; BUDGET PROBE: two PCM voices sounding, both from a BAKED (one-shot) sample.
; budget-2v uses a looped sample, which the exporter can never bake, so its mix
; ticks carry the 16.16 resampler. This is the same shape with the resampler
; out — the `nr` loops the generator already emits — and the difference between
; the two runs is what per-note pitch costs at the sample rate.
(def blip :sample :file "blip.wav")
(pcm1 blip :tempo 120 :oct 4 :len 16 :vel 15
  c c c c  c c c c  c c c c  c c c c
  c c c c  c c c c  c c c c  c c c c)
(pcm2 blip :tempo 120 :oct 5 :len 16 :vel 15
  c c c c  c c c c  c c c c  c c c c
  c c c c  c c c c  c c c c  c c c c)
